.TH u8b_diff 3 "Version 1.0" "December 2023" "lib/utf8"
.SH NAME
u8b_diff \- Compare two UTF-8 strings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/utf8.h>
.sp
.BI "int u8b_diff(const char* x1, size_t n1, const char* x2, size_t n2)"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The function .BR u8b_diff () compares two UTF-8 strings. The function takes the following parameters:
.sp
1. The first string to be compared.
2. The length of the first string.
3. The second string to be compared.
4. The length of the second string.
.sp
The function returns an integer indicating the result of the comparison.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns 0 if the two strings are equal, a negative integer if the first string is less than the second string, and a positive integer if the first string is greater than the second string.
.SH EXAMPLES
No examples are provided for this function.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B u8_to_wc, u8_len
